==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|reprochier|lang=fro}} (Modern {{term|reprocher|lang=fr}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/rɪˈpɹəʊtʃ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/rɪˈpɹoʊtʃ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-reproach.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|əʊtʃ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|reproaches}}

# A [[mild]] [[rebuke]], or an [[implied]] [[criticism]].
#* {{quote-book
|year=1818
|author=Mary Shelley
|title=Frankenstein
|chapter=4
|url=http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/s/shelley/mary/s53f/chapter4.html
|passage=My father made no '''reproach''' in his letters and only took notice of my science by inquiring into my occupations more particularly than before.}}
# [[disgrace|Disgrace]] or [[shame]].

